hadiths[45]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1556","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Forgive the mistakes of honorable people."""
"1557","Muhammad bin Idris narrated that I heard from those scholars who know this hadith. They say that the mistake of an honorable person should be overlooked until his mistake reaches the limit."
"1558","It is narrated from Abu Ja'far that 'Umar bin Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""If today Qudamah is flogged, then after him no one will be spared,"" and Qudamah, may Allah be pleased with him, was a companion who participated in Badr."
"1559","Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that we were sitting in a gathering with the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) when he said: ""Pledge to me that you will not associate anything with Allah."" Then he recited the verse to them and said: ""Whoever fulfills this pledge, his reward is with Allah, and whoever commits any of these acts and is punished for it, then that (punishment) will be an expiation for him. And whoever commits any of these acts and Allah conceals it for him, then his matter is with Allah; if He wills, He will forgive him, and if He wills, He will punish him."""
"1560","It is narrated from Qabeesah bin Dhu’ayb (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “If someone drinks alcohol, flog him. If he drinks again, then flog him again. If he drinks again, then flog him again. If he still drinks, then kill him.” Az-Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) did not know whether the Prophet (ﷺ) gave the order to kill after the third or the fourth time. Then a man was brought who had drunk alcohol and the Prophet (ﷺ) had him flogged. Then he was brought again and the Prophet (ﷺ) had him flogged again. Then he was brought again for drinking alcohol and the Prophet (ﷺ) had him flogged again and did not kill him, and this became a concession (from killing)."
"1561","It is narrated from Qabeesah bin Dhu’ayb (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""If he drinks alcohol, then flog him."""
"1562","Abdur Rahman bin Azhar (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that I saw the Prophet (ﷺ) in the year of Hunain asking about the departure of Khalid bin Walid (may Allah be pleased with him), so I also started walking ahead of the Prophet (ﷺ) asking about Khalid’s camel-litter, until the Prophet (ﷺ) reached him and he was in an injured state. Then a drunkard was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ), so he said: “Beat him.” The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) beat him with their hands, sandals, and the edges of their garments, and threw dust on him. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Rebuke him (say harsh words to him).” So the Companions rebuked him, then the Prophet (ﷺ) let him go. Abdur Rahman bin Azhar said: Then when Abu Bakr’s (may Allah be pleased with him) caliphate came, he asked those who had participated in the beating during the time of the Prophet (ﷺ), and they informed him of forty lashes, so Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) prescribed forty lashes for drinking wine during his lifetime. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) also kept it at forty, until when people began to drink wine excessively, he consulted and then prescribed eighty lashes."
"1563","It is narrated from Thawr bin Zayd Al-Daylami that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) sought advice regarding the one who drinks alcohol. Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""We think that the one who drinks alcohol should be given eighty (80) lashes, because when he drinks alcohol, he becomes intoxicated, and when he becomes intoxicated, he speaks nonsense (utters incoherent words), and when he speaks nonsense, he fabricates slander (false accusations)."" Or as he said. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave eighty (80) lashes to the one who drank alcohol."
"1564","It is narrated from Abu Ja'far Muhammad bin Ali that Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) struck Walid with a whip that had two sides."
"1565","Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came out towards him and said: “I detected the smell of alcohol from such-and-such person, and he claims that he drank tila’ (thick syrup). I will investigate what he drank; if it is intoxicating, I will flog him.” Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) carried out the full prescribed punishment on him."
"1566","It is narrated from Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) that when Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) came out to lead the funeral prayer, Sa’ib heard him say: ""I have smelled alcohol from Ubaidullah and his companions. I will investigate what they have drunk; if it is intoxicating, I will enforce the prescribed punishment (hadd) upon them."" Sa’ib bin Yazid says that he was present there at the time when the punishment was carried out on them."
"1567","Yahya bin Jurayj said: I asked Ata (may Allah have mercy on him), ""Will the legal punishment (hadd) be imposed if the smell of wine is detected?"" Ata (may Allah have mercy on him) replied: ""The smell comes from that wine in which there is harm (intoxication). So, if many people drink the same kind of wine and only one of them becomes intoxicated, then the full punishment of lashes will be imposed on all of them."" Imam Shafi'i (may Allah have mercy on him) said: Ata's statement is exactly like the statement of Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both)."
"1568","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that Ali bin Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, said: ""Whoever is brought to me for drinking wine or intoxicating nabidh, I will certainly impose the punishment of lashes upon him."""
"1569","It is narrated from ‘Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: “Learn from me, learn from me. Allah Almighty has prescribed a way for women. If an unmarried man commits fornication with an unmarried woman, each of them is to receive one hundred lashes and exile for one year. And if a married man and a married woman commit adultery, then one hundred lashes and stoning (to death).”"
"1570","Imam Shafi’i, may Allah have mercy on him, said: A trustworthy narrator informed me that Hasan used to mention Hittan al-Ruqashi as an intermediary between himself and ‘Ubadah, may Allah be pleased with him. Now, I do not know whether ‘Abd al-Wahhab, may Allah have mercy on him, mentioned this intermediary between the two of them. I checked my original book, but it was not present in it. Or perhaps, since I wrote this book, its original has been missing from me."
"1571","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrated that he heard Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) say: ""Stoning is obligatory according to the command of Allah's Book upon the person, whether man or woman, who commits adultery after marriage, when it is proven by valid Shariah witnesses, or there is pregnancy, or someone confesses himself."""
"1572","Saeed bin Musayyib (may Allah have mercy on him) narrates that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Beware lest you forget the verse of stoning, and (after a long time has passed) someone says, 'We do not find two prescribed punishments in the Qur'an.' The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) carried out stoning, and we also stoned. By Him in Whose hand is my soul! If I were not afraid that people would say that Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) has added to the Book of Allah, I would have written it: 'When a married man and a married woman commit adultery, stone them both.' Indeed, we have recited this."""
"1573","It is narrated from Abu Huraira and Zaid bin Khalid (may Allah be pleased with them) that a man stated that his son had committed adultery with another man's wife. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""I will judge between you according to the Book of Allah."" Then he (ﷺ) ordered that his son be given one hundred lashes and exiled for one year. Then the Prophet (ﷺ) ordered Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) to go to the woman in the morning; if she confessed to adultery, then she should be stoned. When the woman confessed, Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) stoned her."
"1574","It is narrated from Abu Huraira and Zaid bin Khalid Al-Juhani (may Allah be pleased with them) that two men brought their dispute before the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). One of them said: ""O Messenger of Allah! Judge between us according to the Book of Allah."" The other, who was more understanding of the two, said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)! Judge between us according to the Book of Allah, and allow me to speak regarding this matter."" The Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Speak."" The man said: ""My son was working as a laborer with this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son would be stoned to death, so I gave him one hundred sheep and a slave girl as ransom for my son. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they informed me that for my son the punishment is one hundred lashes and one year of exile, and the punishment of stoning is for his wife."" Upon this, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul! I will judge between you according to the Book of Allah. Your sheep and your slave girl will be returned to you."" Then he (ﷺ) had the son flogged with one hundred lashes and exiled for one year, and he ordered Anas Al-Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him) to go to the wife of the other man; if she confessed, she should be stoned. The woman confessed, and she was stoned."
"1575","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Prophet (ﷺ) stoned to death a pair of Jews who had committed adultery."
"1576","It is narrated from Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hunaif (may Allah have mercy on him) that a man said: One of them was big-bellied, and the other said: a cripple (disabled) who lived in the neighborhood of Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him), committed adultery with a woman and she became pregnant. The accusation of adultery was placed upon that woman, and when she was questioned, she confessed. Then the Prophet ﷺ gave a ruling regarding her. One of them said: She was beaten with a branch of date-palm (which had a hundred twigs), and the other narrated “Ithkal” instead of “Athkool” (both words have the same meaning)."
"1577","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that I heard Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) saying that stoning (rajm) is obligatory in the Book of Allah for any married person, male or female, who commits adultery, provided that proper Shariah evidence is established, or the woman becomes pregnant, or they confess."
"1578","It is narrated from Abu Waqid Al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him) that Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was in Syria when a man came to him and said that he had found a man with his wife. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent Abu Waqid Al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him) to the man's wife to inquire about the matter. When he came to her, there were other women sitting with her. He told her what her husband had said about her to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), and also told her that she would not be held accountable based solely on his statement. He began to advise her with such words so that she might disagree with her husband's statement, but she refused to disagree and remained firm in her confession. Then Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) gave the order regarding her, and she was stoned."
"1579","Ubaidullah bin Abi Yazid narrated from his father that a man married a woman who had a daughter from her previous husband, and that man had a son from another wife. The boy committed adultery with the girl and she became visibly pregnant. When Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Makkah, this matter was presented before him. He questioned both of them and they confessed. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) imposed the punishment of lashes on both of them, and encouraged them to marry each other, but the boy refused."
"1580","It is narrated from Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""When any of your slave girls commits adultery, and her adultery becomes evident, then impose the prescribed punishment of lashes on her, but do not reproach her. If she commits adultery again and it becomes evident, then again impose the prescribed punishment of lashes on her and do not curse her. If she commits adultery a third time and it becomes evident, then sell her, even if it is for the price of a rope of hair."""
"1581","It is narrated from Hasan bin Muhammad bin Ali that Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her), the daughter of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), carried out the prescribed punishment on her slave woman who had committed adultery."
"1582","Yahya bin Hatib narrated that when Hatib passed away, he freed from among his slaves anyone who had performed prayers and kept fasts. He had a Nubian slave woman who had also performed prayers and kept fasts, and she was a non-Arab. Her pregnancy troubled him. He went to Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) and informed him of this matter. Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""You never bring good news,"" and this statement troubled him. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) sent a message to the slave woman and asked, ""Are you pregnant?"" She replied, ""Yes, from Mar'ush in exchange for two dirhams (due to committing adultery)."" It was as if she was not hiding the matter out of ignorance. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) encountered Ali, Uthman, and Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with them) and said, ""Advise me."" Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting reclining, and Ali and Abdur Rahman bin Awf (may Allah be pleased with them) said, ""The hadd (punishment) will be enforced upon her."" Then he (Umar) said, ""O Uthman, advise me."" He replied, ""Your two brothers have already advised you."" He said, ""Advise me."" So he said, ""In my opinion, she considers this matter light due to not knowing (its seriousness), and the hadd is only enforced upon one who knows its prohibition."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""You have spoken the truth. By Him in Whose hand is my soul, the hadd is only for the one who knows."" Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered her to be flogged one hundred lashes and exiled for one year."
"1583","Narrated from Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""A hand is cut off for a quarter dinar or more."""
"1584","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) cut off the hand of a thief for stealing a shield whose value was three dirhams."
"1585","It is narrated from Umrah bint Abd al-Rahman that during the time of Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him), a thief stole an orange. Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) ordered that its value be assessed, and it was determined to be three dirhams, at the rate of twelve dirhams per dinar, so he had the thief's hand cut off. Imam Malik (may Allah have mercy on him) said: And this is the orange that people eat."
"1586","It is narrated from Humaid At-Tawil that he heard Qatadah (may Allah have mercy on him) asking Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) about cutting off the hand. So Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I went to Abu Bakr As-Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him), and he cut off the hand of a thief for something which I would not like to take even for three dirhams."""
"1587","It is narrated from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) that the hand is cut off for a quarter dinar or more."
"1588","It is narrated from ‘Amrah bint ‘Abd al-Rahman that when ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) set out towards Makkah, two freed slave women and the slave of the son of ‘Abdullah ibn Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with them) were with her. ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) sent a sheet with designs on it to those two slave women, wrapped and sewn in a green cloth. ‘Amrah said: (On the way) the slave undid the stitching, took out the sheet, and put a bag or a sheepskin in its place, then sewed it up again. When the two slave women reached Madinah, they handed over the trust to the family. When they undid the stitching and looked, they found a sheepskin instead of the sheet. They asked the slave women, and they mentioned the matter (of suspicion about the slave) to Umm al-Mu’minin, Lady ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her). Then ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) had his hand cut off and said: “A hand is cut off for a quarter dinar or more.”"
"1589","Abdur Rahman bin Qasim narrates from his father that a man from Yemen, whose one hand and one foot were cut off, came to Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) and complained that the ruler of Yemen had wronged him. He used to pray at night, so Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""By your father's oath! Your night is not the night of thieves."" Then the jewelry of Abu Bakr's (may Allah be pleased with him) wife, Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her), was stolen, so this man also searched with the people and said: ""O Allah! Destroy the one who has stolen from such righteous householders."" Then they found the necklace with a goldsmith, (who said that) this same man with the cut limbs had brought it. The Yemeni thief confessed or it was proven by testimony, so Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) cut off his (remaining) left hand as well, and said: ""By Allah! The cunning curse he used to invoke upon himself seemed harsher to me than his theft."""
"1590","It is narrated from Safwan bin Abdullah bin Safwan that someone said to Safwan bin Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him): ""Whoever has not migrated is ruined."" So Safwan (may Allah be pleased with him) came to Madinah and placed his cloak under his head and slept in the mosque. A thief came and took the cloak from under his head. Safwan (may Allah be pleased with him) caught the thief and brought him to the Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered and his hand was cut off. Then Safwan (may Allah be pleased with him), feeling pity, said: ""That was not my intention; I give the cloak to him as charity."" So the Prophet ﷺ said: ""Why did you not do this before bringing him to me?"""
"1591","It is narrated from Tawus, may Allah have mercy on him, from the Prophet ﷺ, similar to the hadith of Imam Malik."
"1592","It is narrated from Yahya bin Abdur Rahman bin Hatib that the slaves of Hatib stole a camel belonging to a man from the Muzaina tribe and slaughtered it. This matter was brought before Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him), so he ordered Kathir bin Salt to cut off their hands. Then Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""I think you should bring them to me. By Allah! I will impose such a fine on you that it will be a hardship for you."" Then he asked the man from the Muzaina tribe: ""What is the price of your she-camel?"" He said: ""Four hundred dirhams."" Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""Give him eight hundred dirhams."""
"1593","It is narrated from Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when his runaway slave committed theft, Sa'id bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him), the governor of Madinah, refused to cut off his hand. Then Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) ordered his hand to be cut off, and his hand was cut off."
"1594","It is narrated from Sa’ib bin Yazid (may Allah be pleased with him) that Ubaidullah bin Amr al-Hadrami brought his slave to Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) and said: ""Cut off his hand, he has committed theft."" Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) asked: ""What did he steal?"" He said: ""He stole my wife's mirror, which is worth sixty dirhams."" So Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said to them: ""Let him go, his hand will not be cut off; he was your servant and he stole your property."""
"1595","Amr bin Shu'aib (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Prophet (ﷺ) that he (ﷺ) said: ""The hand is not to be cut for (stealing) hanging fruit. However, when it is gathered in the threshing floor (an open place), then the hand is to be cut for it."""
"1596","Rafi' bin Khadij (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated that he heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) say: ""The hand is not to be cut off for fruit or the pit of a date."""
"1597","Through another chain as well, it is narrated from Rafi' bin Khadij, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, similar to the previous hadith."
"1598","Ali bin Husain (may Allah have mercy on him) narrated: By Allah, the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) did not gouge out eyes, and did nothing except cut off the hands and feet of those who herded the milking camels."
"1599","It is narrated from Salih, the freed slave of Tuamah, that regarding bandits, Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When they commit murder and also loot wealth, they will be killed and crucified; and when they commit murder but do not loot wealth, they will be killed but not crucified; and when they loot wealth but do not commit murder, their hands and feet will be cut off from opposite sides; and when they only frighten travelers without looting wealth, they will be exiled."
"1600","Amr bin Dinar stated that everything is in the Qur'an or for it as He willed. Ibn Jurayj said, except for the statement of Allah Almighty: ""Indeed, the penalty for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger..."" (__QUR_5_33__), that there is no choice given in it. Imam Shafi'i, may Allah have mercy on him, also said as Ibn Jurayj and others have said: ""Indeed, the penalty for those who wage war against Allah and His Messenger..."" (__QUR_5_33__). I say that this issue is regarding the one who wages war."
